    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0182" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/563½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-30">August 30, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Navy Department has just
                    informed me that Admiral Leahy has an appointment with the President at 11:15
                    this morning. If you are still at the White House at that time you and Admiral
                    Leahy may care to speak to the President in regard to the question of the U. S.
                    S. <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> proceeding to Shanghai.</p>
                <p>A memorandum in regard to the <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> case is
                        attached.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d213-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="35" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
